message: 'If you use this engine in research or a report, please cite it as below.'
title: 'dpdp-webscan'
type: software
authors:
  - name: 'StateCheck Security'
    website: 'https://statechecksecurity.com'
version: '1.0.0'
date-released: '2026-11-04'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/statecheck-security/dpdp-webscan'
url: 'https://statechecksecurity.com/scan'
abstract: >-
  The engine behind the DPDPA Website Check. It loads a public website in headless
  Chromium and records what the site does before a visitor makes a choice: trackers and
  identifiers that load first, how the consent banner behaves on reject, what forms
  collect and where they send it, and whether the site publishes a privacy contact, a
  way to make rights requests and a grievance period. Each check is mapped to a section
  of India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 or a rule of the DPDP Rules,
  2025. It emits check ids and evidence only, never a score, and it is not legal advice.
keywords:
  - DPDP Act
  - DPDPA
  - India
  - privacy
  - website scanner
  - consent banner
  - trackers
  - cookies
